{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented RED-first in worktree feat/9416-rename-overlap.\n\nReference set derived with BOTH tools and reconciled:\n- Serena find_referencing_symbols (VerifyConfig/overlap_enabled) found 5 structural attribute reads: llm/enrich_drain.py maybe_drain, llm/plan_review/__init__.py _run_plan_review, and 3 test assertions.\n- grep -rni found 5 MORE sites the LSP cannot see: the _SECTIONS string coercer key in _config_schema.py, rebar.toml, both tests/golden/config_surface.json entries, docs/adr/0037 line 64, plus the field declaration and two prose comments. Serena alone would have shipped a broken _SECTIONS key and a stale golden.\n\nBoth planning-agent claims verified independently:\n1. 'undocumented outside the config schema' HOLDS - docs/config.md has zero 'overlap' occurrences; the only doc mention is docs/adr/0037:64; docs/env-vars.md had no REBAR_VERIFY_* row at all.\n2. The AC self-correction DID land - AC5 mandates a case-insensitive grep and correctly lists item (4) as the UPPERCASE _LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES key. No plan defect to fix.\n\nChange: verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets is now the canonical key; verify.overlap_enabled and REBAR_VERIFY_OVERLAP_ENABLED are PERMANENT aliases (_ALIASES + two _permanent registry rows + one _LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES row). docs/config.md gains the missing inventory entry and the back-compat line; docs/env-vars.md regenerated (the new alias row appears there, and --check is clean).\n\nNot pushed to Gerrit per instruction."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785698272724680001,"uuid":"d8b8660b-10b4-4b4a-82ef-cb8409b394cd"}